    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d522">

                <pb facs="0691" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg621"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Pike.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 8, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of September No. 60) has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>The unfavorable aspect of our affairs under which it was written has given place
                    to another which illustrates the strength and vigor of the Union and the loyalty
                    and enthusiasm of the people.</p>
                <p>The repulsion of the insurgents from Maryland, Cincinnati, and Ohio, ; with the
                    recent triumphs of the national arms in Missouri and Mississippi, need no
                    explanations to show their importance.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James S. Pike</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
